s=dict(action='continue',rationale='Register the sourced two-line core map and investigate a distinct automatic-configuration continuation premise. The read question remains a surface; no liveness obligation is inferred from a finite wait.',sources=sources,map_path='core-map.json',question=q,feedback=dict(ref_ids=['S-nodecontract','S-readycontract','S-autoleave','S-abort','S-jointcontract'],answered='ReadIndex explicitly permits unnoticed loss and requires caller retry, so missing read completion by itself is not a grounded violation. The Ready interface requires Entries persisted before synchronous Messages, which is stricter than the README same-batch overlap wording; a future driver can obey both by persisting before send. Automatic joint exit is separately promised by the configuration API and is initiated by appliedTo; transfer rejection and retry ownership therefore merit their own question.',remaining=['Read configuration-commit legal history, including documented early Advance, remains open without a completion claim','For automatic joint exit, close trigger coverage and execute a legal transfer/application overlap before fixing any obligation'],understanding='updated',rationale='Caller contracts narrow the original reading question; separate API semantics supply a more specific continuation discriminator.'))
